// Litter tray: observable-signal example for `rounded_box` / `rounded_rect`
// (task #5201) — a rectangular tray with the 4 plan-view (vertical) corners
// rounded to `corner_r`.
//
// `rounded_box` is origin-centred on all 3 axes (same anchor as `box`/
// `box_centered`), so `translate(rounded_box(...), 0mm, 0mm, height/2)`
// lifts the base onto the z=0 build plate while staying x/y-centred — the
// same centred-solid-onto-build-plate idiom as `fdm_bracket.ri`, just along
// one axis instead of all three.
//
// `rim` cross-checks the 2D `rounded_rect` profile: extruding the
// rounded-rectangle footprint by the tray's `height` produces the same
// rounded-corner solid as `rounded_box` itself (volume equality is the
// numeric signal asserted end-to-end in
// crates/reify-eval/tests/rounded_primitives_e2e.rs).
//
// This file is auto-covered by crates/reify-compiler/tests/examples_smoke.rs
// (recursive examples/*.ri compile-clean walk; zero Error diagnostics).

structure def LitterTray {
    param width: Length = 480mm
    param depth: Length = 260mm
    param height: Length = 80mm
    param corner_r: Length = 25mm

    // Base sits on the z=0 build plate; x/y stay centred on the origin.
    let tray = translate(rounded_box(width, depth, height, corner_r), 0mm, 0mm, height / 2)

    // Same footprint as `tray`, built from the 2D profile + extrude instead
    // of the boolean-compose solid constructor directly.
    let rim = extrude(rounded_rect(width, depth, corner_r), height)
}
